Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:30:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] =?UTF-8?q?feat(governance):=20VK-implies-user=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20derive=20userID=20from=20hierarchyVK.UserID?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a request comes in via a virtual key whose UserID FK is set, run
user-level governance for that user. Identity precedence:

  1. evaluationRequest.UserID — explicitly set by upstream (e.g.
     enterprise auth middleware extracting from token / header)
  2. hierarchyVK.UserID — VK has been pinned to a user via the
     user_id FK added in 0002

When neither is set, the user step short-circuits with DecisionAllow.

No new middleware, no new context keys, no new headers. The FK on
TableVirtualKey is the binding mechanism.
---
 plugins/governance/main.go | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/governance/main.go b/plugins/governance/main.go
index 879989bc5..eda1e9d85 100644
--- a/plugins/governance/main.go
+++ b/plugins/governance/main.go
@@ -1269,9 +1269,18 @@ func (p *GovernancePlugin) EvaluateGovernanceRequest(ctx *schemas.BifrostContext
 		}
 	}
 
-	// Step 4: User-level governance (enterprise-only).
+	// Step 4: User-level governance. Identity precedence:
+	//   1. evaluationRequest.UserID set upstream (e.g. by enterprise auth middleware)
+	//   2. hierarchyVK.UserID — VK has been pinned to a user via the user_id FK
+	// When neither is set, EvaluateUserRequest short-circuits with DecisionAllow.
 	if !skipBudgetsAndRateLimits && result.Decision == DecisionAllow {
-		result = p.resolver.EvaluateUserRequest(ctx, evaluationRequest.UserID, evaluationRequest)
+		userID := evaluationRequest.UserID
+		if userID == "" && hierarchyVK != nil && hierarchyVK.UserID != nil {
+			userID = *hierarchyVK.UserID
+		}
+		if userID != "" {
+			result = p.resolver.EvaluateUserRequest(ctx, userID, evaluationRequest)
+		}
 	}
 
 	// Check the actual MCP tools injected into the request against the VK MCPConfigs.
